__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
tools/ui-smoke/pwenv/
frontend-v2/node_modules/
# raggity's index directory. `raggity serve`/`ingest` creates it in the CWD when
# no config points elsewhere, so running the RAG sidecar from a checkout drops a
# LanceDB index here. It is derived data — never source.
.raggity/

# internal working notes — never published. `docs/*` rather than `docs/` so the
# one shipped guide can be re-included below: a file inside an excluded
# DIRECTORY cannot be re-included, no matter what the negation says.
docs/*
# the agent-integration guide is user-facing documentation, not a working note —
# it is shipped in the wheel/repo and pointed at from the legacy UI.
!docs/AGENTS.md
# A SPECIFICATION is a deliverable that a reviewer, a future maintainer and CI
# all have to be able to read, not a working note that only exists on one
# machine — so the vLLM engine spec is shipped.
#
# Deliberately a FILE exception and not `!docs/design/`. Re-including the
# directory drags in every other design note on this machine (`CONSTITUTION.md`,
# `UI-REWORK-PLAN.md`, `research/`), which is the opposite of what the rule above
# is for: those are the owner's working notes and were never published. Naming
# the file means adding a note to `docs/design/` cannot publish it by accident.
!docs/design/2026-09-25-vllm-engine-spec.md
